    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "sql",
      "content": "1SELECT *\n2FROM Customers\n3INNER JOIN Orders\n4ON Customers.first_name = Orders.customer_id;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the INNER JOIN condition references the wrong column name in the Customers table."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "How to Fix It?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Update the join condition to reference the correct column name i.e., customer_id."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "sql",
      "content": "1SELECT *\n2FROM Customers\n3INNER JOIN Orders\n4ON Customers.customer_id = Orders.customer_id;"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
